# PAWPLE CURSOR RULES (STRICT ENFORCEMENT)

You are building Pawple — a calm, premium, emotionally restrained pet journaling & meetup app.

Pawple is NOT a traditional social media product.

It should feel:
• warm
• calm
• breathable
• emotionally soft
• premium
• human
• pet-first
• Apple-inspired

NOT:
❌ engagement-driven
❌ loud
❌ cluttered
❌ heavily decorated
❌ utility-heavy
❌ influencer-oriented

ALWAYS follow these rules.
NEVER deviate unless explicitly instructed.

-----------------------------------------------------
🧠 CORE PRODUCT PHILOSOPHY
-----------------------------------------------------

Pawple should feel like:
“A quiet collection of saved pet memories.”

NOT:
❌ Instagram clone
❌ Pinterest aesthetic
❌ scrapbook craft project
❌ event management app
❌ creator platform

RULE:
Every screen should prioritize:
1. the pet/content
2. emotional warmth
3. calm composition

NOT:
the design system itself.

-----------------------------------------------------
🧠 COMPOSITION PHILOSOPHY (STRICT)
-----------------------------------------------------

Screens should feel:
• inevitable
• emotionally calm
• breathable
• softly composed
• visually quiet
• premium through restraint

Whitespace should feel:
• intentional
• calming
• balanced

NOT:
❌ empty
❌ excessive
❌ mechanically spaced

RULE:
When uncertain, REMOVE rather than ADD.

-----------------------------------------------------

AVOID:
❌ helper text overload
❌ excessive labels
❌ decorative UI
❌ stacked chips everywhere
❌ loud visual hierarchy
❌ dense forms
❌ visible configuration systems
❌ excessive segmentation

-----------------------------------------------------

FAVOR:
✅ compressed interactions
✅ hidden complexity
✅ placeholders over explanations
✅ progressive disclosure
✅ natural language
✅ calm layouts
✅ emotionally invisible guidance

-----------------------------------------------------
✍️ UX WRITING PHILOSOPHY
-----------------------------------------------------

Pawple copy should be:
• short
• human
• obvious
• emotionally quiet
• natural

Avoid:
❌ long labels
❌ UX-writer-heavy phrasing
❌ explanatory helper text
❌ over-emotional narration
❌ instructional writing

Prefer:
✅ one-word labels
✅ compressed language
✅ example-driven placeholders

-----------------------------------------------------

GOOD:
“Meetup”
“Open to”
“Time”
“Joining paws”

BAD:
“What should nearby paws call this meetup?”
“Who’s this meetup best suited for?”
“When should nearby paws arrive?”

-----------------------------------------------------

RULE:
Placeholders should guide naturally.

Prefer:
examples over explanations.

-----------------------------------------------------
🔤 TYPOGRAPHY HIERARCHY (STRICT)
-----------------------------------------------------

PRIMARY FONT:
Inter

HANDWRITTEN FONT:
Caveat

-----------------------------------------------------

Inter is used for:
• UI
• buttons
• labels
• inputs
• metadata
• navigation
• settings
• legal text
• meetup UI
• onboarding
• tabs

-----------------------------------------------------

Caveat is ONLY used for:
• handwritten captions
• moment/journal writing
• emotionally personal text

-----------------------------------------------------

NEVER use Caveat for:
❌ buttons
❌ navigation
❌ labels
❌ forms
❌ tabs
❌ metadata
❌ legal text

-----------------------------------------------------

FONT SIZES

BODY / INPUTS:
Inter Regular 16px

LABELS / METADATA:
Inter Medium 14px

BUTTONS:
Inter SemiBold 16px

CARD TITLES:
Inter SemiBold 18px

PAGE TITLES:
Inter SemiBold 30px

HANDWRITTEN CAPTIONS:
Caveat Regular 18–20px

SMALL METADATA:
Inter Regular 12px

BRANDING:
Inter Medium 11px

-----------------------------------------------------
🎨 COLOR SYSTEM (STRICT TOKEN USAGE)
-----------------------------------------------------

ALL colors MUST come from:
theme.colors.*

NEVER hardcode colors except explicit brand colors below.

-----------------------------------------------------

BACKGROUND:
screen → #F5F4F1
card → #FBFAF8

-----------------------------------------------------

TEXT:
primary → #2F2F2F
secondary → #6A6A6A
muted → #7A7A7A
placeholder → #9A9A9A

-----------------------------------------------------

SAGE SYSTEM:
sage → #8FAF9B
sageLight → #E8F1EA
sageDark → #6D8B74

-----------------------------------------------------

HEART PURPLE:
#7B61FF

-----------------------------------------------------

FRAME COLOR:
#7A4F46

Alternative:
#70564B

-----------------------------------------------------

RULE:
Always import:
import { theme } from '../config/theme'

-----------------------------------------------------
📐 SPACING & SAFE AREA SYSTEM
-----------------------------------------------------

STRICT 8PT GRID ONLY:
8, 16, 24, 32, 48, 64

Avoid arbitrary spacing.

-----------------------------------------------------

SCREEN PADDING:
Top → 24px
Horizontal → 20px
Bottom → 32px

-----------------------------------------------------

SECTION GAP:
24px

-----------------------------------------------------

LABEL → INPUT GAP:
8px

-----------------------------------------------------

CARD PADDING:
16px

-----------------------------------------------------

BOTTOM SAFE AREA:
minimum 32px

-----------------------------------------------------

RULE:
Content must NEVER:
❌ collide with notch
❌ touch gesture area
❌ feel cramped vertically

-----------------------------------------------------

ALL screens MUST use:
SafeAreaView

-----------------------------------------------------

ScrollViews MUST use:
contentContainerStyle={{
  paddingTop: 24,
  paddingHorizontal: 20,
  paddingBottom: 32,
  flexGrow: 1,
}}

-----------------------------------------------------
🧩 COMPONENT SYSTEM
-----------------------------------------------------

BUTTONS:
• minHeight 48px
• borderRadius 22px
• Inter SemiBold 16px
• backgroundColor: theme.colors.sage

-----------------------------------------------------

INPUTS:
• borderRadius 16px
• minHeight 48px
• paddingVertical 14px
• paddingHorizontal 16px
• backgroundColor: theme.colors.background.card
• Inter Regular 16px

-----------------------------------------------------

CARDS:
• borderRadius 22px
• backgroundColor: theme.colors.background.card
• subtle shadow only
• marginBottom 24px

-----------------------------------------------------

BOTTOM SHEETS:
• soft appearance only
• handle width 40px
• handle height 4px
• radius 2px
• backdrop rgba(0,0,0,0.35)

-----------------------------------------------------

RULE:
Never use default React Native styling.

Everything must feel:
• soft
• calm
• premium
• restrained

-----------------------------------------------------
🖼️ FEED IMAGE & FRAME PHILOSOPHY
-----------------------------------------------------

Moment posts should feel like:
“printed memories softly placed on paper.”

NOT:
❌ image assets with overlays
❌ scrapbook templates
❌ graphic-designed cards

-----------------------------------------------------

RULE:
The frame ALWAYS exists OUTSIDE the image.

NEVER place:
❌ sketch lines
❌ doodles
❌ borders
❌ decorative overlays

INSIDE the photograph.

-----------------------------------------------------

FRAME RULES:
• warm maroon-brown only
• subtle imperfection
• slightly hand-drawn
• 2px max stroke
• ~75% opacity

-----------------------------------------------------

TILT RULES:
ONLY:
• image
• outer frame

may tilt.

-----------------------------------------------------

NEVER tilt:
❌ captions
❌ metadata
❌ branding
❌ card container

-----------------------------------------------------

ALL posts MUST maintain:
the SAME orientation direction.

Tilt:
-1.5deg maximum.

-----------------------------------------------------

RULE:
The pet/photo is ALWAYS the emotional focus.

The frame should support the memory quietly,
NOT dominate visually.

-----------------------------------------------------
📸 FEED CARD COMPOSITION
-----------------------------------------------------

Feed cards should feel:
• breathable
• calm
• handcrafted
• emotionally restrained

-----------------------------------------------------

IMAGE RATIO:
4:5 portrait

-----------------------------------------------------

IMAGE DOMINANCE:
~82% of card height

-----------------------------------------------------

BOTTOM CONTENT ORDER:
1. handwritten caption
2. pet name
3. metadata
4. subtle pawple branding

-----------------------------------------------------

HEART & SHARE:
• always OUTSIDE the card
• no counts
• no comments
• no reposts
• no social metrics

-----------------------------------------------------

HEART INTERACTION:
• pulse twice on first like
• fill purple
• remain purple until unliked

Animation:
soft only.
180–260ms.

-----------------------------------------------------

PAWPLE BRANDING:
• lowercase only
• subtle
• bottom-right
• never watermark-like

-----------------------------------------------------
🚫 ANTI-CLUTTER ENFORCEMENT
-----------------------------------------------------

Always minimize visible UI.

Hide complexity whenever possible.

Prefer:
• bottom sheets
• progressive disclosure
• collapsed interactions
• compressed UI

-----------------------------------------------------

Avoid:
❌ always-visible options
❌ giant forms
❌ helper paragraphs
❌ excessive chips
❌ configuration-heavy screens
❌ visual noise

-----------------------------------------------------

RULE:
If the same idea is already communicated naturally,
DO NOT create additional UI for it.

-----------------------------------------------------
🗄️ SUPABASE & DATA
-----------------------------------------------------

Always wrap DB calls in try/catch.

Log exact Supabase errors:
console.error('[Supabase]', error)

-----------------------------------------------------

Always fetch:
supabase.auth.getUser()

before write operations.

-----------------------------------------------------

RULE:
Never modify:
❌ schemas
❌ RLS
❌ queries
❌ insert/update logic

unless explicitly instructed.

-----------------------------------------------------
🤖 AI OUTPUT BEHAVIOR
-----------------------------------------------------

ALWAYS:
• output complete runnable files
• preserve architecture
• preserve navigation
• preserve Supabase logic
• preserve state management

-----------------------------------------------------

WHEN MODIFYING UI:
Only change:
• styling
• spacing
• composition
• visual hierarchy

DO NOT break:
• logic
• data flow
• interactions

-----------------------------------------------------

ADD:
helpful beginner-friendly comments explaining WHY.

-----------------------------------------------------

MENTALLY TEST:
• imports
• theme mapping
• spacing
• safe areas
• prop usage
• navigation

before outputting.

-----------------------------------------------------
🚫 STRICT PROHIBITIONS
-----------------------------------------------------

❌ hardcoded colors
❌ hardcoded fonts
❌ arbitrary spacing
❌ Caveat outside emotional text
❌ visual clutter
❌ helper text overload
❌ dense layouts
❌ loud gradients
❌ strong shadows
❌ engagement metrics
❌ comments
❌ follower systems
❌ popularity systems
❌ overlapping safe areas
❌ navigation rewrites
❌ deleting architecture without instruction
❌ partial code outputs
❌ over-designed scrapbook aesthetics

-----------------------------------------------------
FINAL PRINCIPLE
-----------------------------------------------------

Pawple should feel:
like a calm emotional product,
not a designed interface.

TECH STACK: Expo SDK 51+ | React Native 0.74+ | React Navigation 6+ | Supabase JS v2 | react-native-safe-area-context
HEART ANIMATION: Use simple state-driven scale transform (Animated API). Pulse twice on first like. Duration: 200ms. No external libraries required.

FRAME IMPLEMENTATION: Use a styled View with subtle border-radius variation or a lightweight SVG path. Do NOT use image overlays, heavy shaders, or third-party frame packages.

When uncertain:
REMOVE rather than ADD.

-----------------------------------------------------
🆕 MEETUP & PROFILE DESIGN SYSTEM (LATEST)
-----------------------------------------------------
These rules apply specifically to the Meetup Cards, Pet Profile Hero, and My Meetups sections. They override general component rules where there is a conflict.

MEETUP CARD COLORS:
- Card Background: #FFFCF8
- Card Border: #F1E8DF
- Title Color: #6E8E73 (Sage Green variant for Meetup Titles ONLY)
- Primary Button: #9EB8A0 (Sage Green)
- Muted Accent (Labels/Icons): #8EA88F
- Date/Time Text: #4A403B
- Participant Text: #6B625C

MEETUP TYPOGRAPHY OVERRIDES:
- Meetup Card Title: Inter SemiBold 22px (Overrides general Card Title 18px)
- "YOUR MEETUP" Label: Inter Medium 11px, Letter Spacing 1px, Uppercase, #8EA88F
- Date & Time: Inter Medium 16px, #4A403B
- Location/Distance: Inter Regular 14px, #8EA88F

PET PROFILE HERO OVERRIDES:
- Pet Name: Inter SemiBold 26-28px, #3A312E
- Pet Subtitle (Breed • Age): Inter Medium 15px, #666
- Bio: Italicized, #888, Max 100 chars.
- Companion Badge: #9EB8A0 background, White text, rounded pill.

MEETUP ARCHITECTURE RULES:
- Meetups belong to PETS, not users. 
- Always use `meetup_hosts` and `meetup_participants` junction tables.
- Never show owner/human names on meetup cards. Only show pet names (e.g., "Hosted by Tyson • Peter").
- Mock data must always include at least 1 mock host pet. Participant count must be realistic (Hosts + User + Random Extras). Minimum count is 2.

STRICT MEETUP UI PROHIBITIONS:
- NO system emojis (like 📍) in the location line. Use clean text.
- NO fake "initial" avatars for hosts. Use real photos or just text names.
- NO double paw emojis. Use a single quiet paw or just text.
- NO heavy borders around sections. Use whitespace (24px) to separate.
- NO exclamation marks in the primary button ("You're Going", not "You're Going!").